        "rationale": "Inspected both dialogue lines and supplied-chest approach at desktop and 390px phone scale. Wren, player, Fernling and chest remain visible; actual text fragments clear Next/Done; the live objective is readable in the sidebar (scrollable on phone). The final fixture keeps the player beside the chest rather than inside its image. Generic engine presentation is not a claim of bespoke adventure polish. Compatible #258 schema addition was rerun and the regenerated desktop/phone captures were inspected; owner status is unchanged. Repeated controls and captures after the opt-in orchard interaction priority change; teaching fixture behavior is preserved. Claude reran the real-control captures after battle presentation changes (#389) touched the bound controller and stylesheet sources, and inspected the desktop dialogue and phone supplies captures: speaker, player, companion and chest, the text and the Done control are still unobstructed and the layout is unchanged. Owner status is unchanged. Rebound the retained scene evidence after a change isolated to startup pack-integrity diagnostics; no successful-play scene rendering or layout source changed, and the previously inspected captures retain the same pixels. Claude reran the real-control captures again after the regional atlas (#276) added stylesheet rules to a bound source, and inspected the desktop dialogue capture: speaker, player, companion, chest and the Next control are unobstructed and the layout is unchanged. Owner status is unchanged. Claude reran the real-control captures after the companion-aware dialogue conditions (#277) changed the bound startup source (main.js condition context only), and inspected the desktop dialogue and phone supplies captures: speaker, player, companion, chest, the text and the Done control are unobstructed and the layout is unchanged. Owner status is unchanged. Claude reran the real-control captures after the creature field roles change (#262) touched the bound controller source, and inspected the desktop dialogue and phone dialogue captures: speaker, player, companion, chest, the text and the Next/Done control are unobstructed and the layout is unchanged. Owner status is unchanged. Codex reran the real-control captures after the Voltkit asset manifest and provenance refresh; the scene layout remained unobstructed and the evidence was rebound to the regenerated captures. No scene behavior or layout source changed. Claude reran the real-control captures after the pack-compatibility start-screen error handling (#283) changed the bound startup source (main.js error branches only), and inspected the captures: speaker, player, companion, chest, the text and the Next/Done control are unobstructed and the layout is unchanged. Owner status is unchanged. Reran the real-control desktop and 390px phone captures on the current main baseline after the portal startup-gate refresh; the player, speaker, companion, chest, dialogue and advance control remain visible. This records implementation evidence only; owner acceptance remains deferred. Reran and inspected the real-control desktop and 390px phone captures on the current main baseline after #431 added optional authored NPC reactions; speaker, player, companion, chest, dialogue and advance control remain visible. This records implementation evidence only; owner acceptance remains deferred. Reran real-control desktop/phone captures after #265 conditional decoration and #270 traveler-only reaction binding; inspected desktop first dialogue and phone second dialogue. Existing actors, text and advance controls remain visible; the fixture has no conditional decoration or active reaction. Owner acceptance is unchanged."
